      "versionNonce": 1773853053,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Footprint: 30 ft x 60 ft (1,800 sq ft)\nAll sizes are nominal wall-line modules;\nfinished clear sizes will be smaller.\n\nMaster size includes its attached bath.\n*Common bath size includes a 2' x 2'\nvertical ventilation duct to the roof.\nBlue = window; brown = door leaf.\nOpen gap = access without a door.\n\nKitchen: east window and exterior exhaust.\nUse high-level openable transoms over\nbedroom and kitchen doors for airflow\nto the north-ventilated passage.\nProvide door grilles for puja / pantry.\nDaylight and airflow depend on site,\nclimate and unobstructed openings;\nside windows need open space outside.\n\nAssumes a single floor and south entry.\nNo setbacks, parking or stairs shown.\nSite access and local rules may require\na different layout and footprint.\n\nConcept only: have a local architect /\nengineer verify setbacks, structure,\nventilation, plumbing and safety.",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Footprint: 30 ft x 60 ft (1,800 sq ft)\nAll sizes are nominal wall-line modules;\nfinished clear sizes will be smaller.\n\nMaster size includes its attached bath.\n*Common bath size includes a 2' x 2'\nvertical ventilation duct to the roof.\nBlue = window; brown = door leaf.\nOpen gap = access without a door.\n\nKitchen: east window and exterior exhaust.\nUse high-level openable transoms over\nbedroom and kitchen doors for airflow\nto the north-ventilated passage.\nProvide door grilles for puja / pantry.\nDaylight and airflow depend on site,\nclimate and unobstructed openings;\nside windows need open space outside.\n\nAssumes a single floor and south entry.\nNo setbacks, parking or stairs shown.\nSite access and local rules may require\na different layout and footprint.\n\nConcept only: have a local architect /\nengineer verify setbacks, structure,\nventilation, plumbing and safety.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
